WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.040
[dramatic music]

2
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.080
[Duchovny] Tonight
on "Secrets Declassified"...

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.200
government sites so surprising
or dangerous

4
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.200
that they're kept
from the public--

5
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.000
from a luxury resort hiding
a government doomsday bunker...

6
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.200
- If a bomb drops
on the golf course.

7
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.600
anyone behind the blast doors
would be okay.

8
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.000
- To an explosive factory
where every shift

9
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.800
is life or death...

10
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.960
[Martin] I can't imagine
something more stressful

11
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.680
than trying to disassemble
a thermonuclear warhead.

12
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.120
- And even a fake country
in Virginia

13
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.320
that's really
a CIA training camp.

14
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.480
- When you cross the border
into this fake world.

15
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.280
it's Disney World for adults.

16
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.600
- These are the astonishing
and sometimes terrible places

17
00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.320
built by governments and
the people who work for them.

18
00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.160
It's time to bring them
to light.

19
00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:02.280
♪ ♪

20
00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.000
In West Virginia.
there's a luxury hotel

21
00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.400
for the rich and famous

22
00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.800
that boasts
over 700 guest rooms.

23
00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.560
exclusive restaurants.
an 18-hole golf course.

24
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.360
and a secret underground bunker
primed for Armageddon.

25
00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.120
♪ ♪

26
00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.120
[Hakeem] Nuclear anxiety
is peaking in the 1950s...

27
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.600
and the U.S. president
is concerned

28
00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:31.800
about the safety
of the government

29
00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.680
in the case
of a nuclear attack.

30
00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.600
The government
has commissioned

31
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.200
these bomb-proof havens

32
00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.240
for the president
and his cabinet.

33
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.000
[Duchovny]
Now they want a bunker

34
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.600
for members of Congress--

35
00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.200
somewhere big enough

36
00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.400
to house over
1.000 government officials

37
00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.960
and discreet enough
to keep it secret.

38
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.440
The answer--
a five-star hotel.

39
00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.200
[Hakeem] The Greenbrier
is a luxury resort

40
00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.640
in White Sulphur Springs.
West Virginia.

41
00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:01.360
This place is a slice
of old-school luxury.

42
00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:04.560
where the rich and powerful
come to do business and relax.

43
00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.280
You can find presidents
or celebrities

44
00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.920
sipping drinks at the bar.

45
00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.080
[Duchovny] It sounds
like the perfect place

46
00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.240
to see out World War III.

47
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.840
- It's far enough
from Washington. D.C..

48
00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.800
that hopefully
it could escape the effects

49
00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.920
of a direct nuclear attack
on the capital city

50
00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.400
but also close enough

51
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.800
that people would be able
to escape to it in time.

52
00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.600
[Duchovny]
It's shielded by mountains

53
00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.280
for extra protection.

54
00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.200
- Perhaps what swings it.
literally.

55
00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.720
is the hotel's
golfing facilities.

56
00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.680
Eisenhower is a regular
on the Greenbrier course.

57
00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.320
♪ ♪

58
00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.480
[Duchovny] The government
discreetly approaches

59
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.360
the hotel
for their assistance.

60
00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:43.240
and the management
at the Greenbrier

61
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.120
are happy to oblige.

62
00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.760
The only problem
is keeping it a secret.

63
00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.320
- An immense
construction project

64
00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.680
on the grounds
of the Greenbrier

65
00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.880
is sure to get
the VIP guests gossiping.

66
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.320
So the bunker needs
a cover story.

67
00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.760
[Duchovny] The Greenbrier
gets a brand-new extension--

68
00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.280
the West Virginia Wing.

69
00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.000
Underneath...

70
00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.080
a vast doomsday bunker
unlike any other

71
00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.880
begins to take shape.

72
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.280
[Hakeem] The bunker underneath

73
00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.640
the Greenbrier Hotel

74
00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.000
hosts 153 rooms

75
00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:17.360
spread out
over 112.000 square feet.

76
00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.880
There are two chambers

77
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.200
for the House and the Senate.

78
00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.560
and there is this vast hall

79
00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.160
for joint sessions.

80
00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.080
It's essentially
a giant underground capitol

81
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.200
for the government
to continue functioning

82
00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.000
in the event of a nuclear war.

83
00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.160
- Beyond these chambers
are the facilities you'd expect

84
00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.520
in a top-of-the-range
government survival bunker--

85
00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.240
high-pressure shower
to rinse off nuclear fallout.

86
00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.240
over 1.000 beds
for congressmen and women.

87
00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.200
a hospital. a cafeteria.

88
00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:47.200
and a small arsenal
of handguns.

89
00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.400
[Duchovny] Perhaps
the most impressive features

90
00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:54.040
are two enormous blast doors
to seal Congress inside.

91
00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.520
- Each door is 19 inches thick.
weighs 28 tons.

92
00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:02.240
and they're strong enough
to withstand a nuclear blast

93
00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:04.600
from only 2.000 feet away.

94
00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.000
- If a bomb drops

95
00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.080
on the eighth hole
of the golf course.

96
00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.920
anyone behind the blast doors
will be okay.

97
00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.160
- And these doors are hidden
behind a false wall

98
00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.000
in the exhibition hall
just inches away

99
00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.160
from where guests
are mingling.

100
00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.840
- For 30 years.
the false wall stands firm.

101
00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.000
and the bunker
remains secret...

102
00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:29.760
until 1992. when rumors
finally begin to leak out.

103
00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.640
♪ ♪

104
00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:34.200
[Jesse] Ted Gup
is a investigative reporter

105
00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.800
for "The Washington Post."

106
00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.000
and an anonymous source
tips him off

107
00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.000
that the Greenbrier resort

108
00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:44.240
might not be all that it seems.

109
00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.320
[Duchovny] Gup speaks
to former employees.

110
00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.000
who confirm
that something mysterious

111
00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.880
is hidden beneath
the West Virginia Wing.

112
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.400
But for a genuine scoop.

113
00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.080
Gup needs hard evidence.

114
00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.480
- So he decides to go stay
at the Greenbrier himself

115
00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:02.600
to see if he can get
that final bit of proof.

116
00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.480
[O'Keefe]
When Gup meets the manager.

117
00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.400
he goes straight to the point.

118
00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.200
He asks. "Is there a government
nuclear fallout shelter

119
00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:11.520
under the hotel?"

120
00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.920
Well. the manager
immediately denies this.

121
00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.880
♪ ♪

122
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.600
[Duchovny] Gup doesn't get
the answers he's hoping for.

123
00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.200
but he's determined
not to leave the Greenbrier

124
00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:24.440
without his story.

125
00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:27.200
- Gup visits the office
of a maintenance company

126
00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.200
called Forsyth Associates.

127
00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:30.800
who are supposedly in charge

128
00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:33.000
of maintaining
the Greenbrier TVs.

129
00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.800
When he gets to the offices.
he sees something strange.

130
00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:39.520
[Hakeem] He sees a wall
covered with books

131
00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:43.280
on nuclear war and Armageddon.

132
00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.960
You don't need that
if you're building TV antennas.

133
00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.800
- When he digs deeper.
he finds out

134
00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:50.760
that many of the people
who work at Forsyth Associates

135
00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.800
are former U.S. military
cryptographers

136
00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.480
and radio specialists.

137
00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.840
- Turns out. Forsyth Associates
is just a front company.

138
00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.600
Their real job is maintaining
the communications

139
00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.640
for the bunker.

140
00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.200
[Duchovny]
"The Washington Post"

141
00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:08.920
runs Gup's story
on May 31. 1992.

142
00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.800
♪ ♪

143
00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:15.520
And the Greenbrier's secret
is finally unearthed.

144
00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.800
Within days.
the government goes public

145
00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:20.400
about the Greenbrier bunker...

146
00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.680
and announces
its deactivation.

147
00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.400
- Today the bunker
is a tourist attraction.

148
00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:28.080
For about $50.

149
00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.200
you can go tour the halls
where the American government

150
00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.880
might have been reborn
after Armageddon.

151
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.400
♪ ♪

152
00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.800
- A luxury hotel
might be the perfect place

153
00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:39.680
to hide a government bunker.

154
00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:44.240
but in the 1950s. the CIA has
to hide something much bigger--

155
00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.600
a vast college campus set up

156
00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:50.160
to train the next generation
of super spies.

157
00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:54.960
♪ ♪

158
00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.600
[Sami]
At the dawn of the Cold War.

159
00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:59.200
the CIA realizes
that this is a conflict

160
00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:00.800
that's not going to be fought

161
00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.600
by traditional soldiers
with bullets and bombs

162
00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:06.080
but by covert agents
stealing secrets

163
00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.800
from under the enemy's nose.

164
00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.960
When it comes
to training spies. though.

165
00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.200
the Americans
are on their back foot

166
00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.200
compared to their rivals
at the KGB.

167
00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:17.600
[Andrew] The KGB has
a decades-old infrastructure

168
00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:19.280
for training spies.

169
00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.600
and CIA is relatively new
to the game.

170
00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.800
So they realize that
if they're going to keep up

171
00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:27.040
with their KGB counterparts.
they have to step up big.

172
00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:29.600
[Hakeem] The spy-craft skills
that could save your life

173
00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:33.120
and maybe even your country
isn't something that's taught

174
00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.920
in any college or university.

175
00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:37.800
The CIA brass realize
that their agents

176
00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:40.480
need training to prepare them
for the real world--

177
00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.080
what they're gonna face
out there in the field.

178
00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.200
So. in secret. they set up

179
00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:48.640
a new espionage university.

180
00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.800
[Duchovny] The first step
is finding the right place

181
00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:52.240
for a campus.

182
00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.000
- They need a very large place.

183
00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.400
someplace secluded.
someplace cut off.

184
00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.280
but someplace large enough
with infrastructure enough

185
00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.920
to simulate the activities
of a normal city.

186
00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.520
[Duchovny]
They find it

187
00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:07.560
at a former naval base
called Camp Peary.

188
00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.600
- It stretches
for 9.000 acres--

189
00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.960
more than half the size
of Manhattan.

190
00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:13.320
♪ ♪

191
00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.000
[Sami]
To the outside world.

192
00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.600
Camp Peary remains
a regular naval base.

193
00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.800
But behind its fences.
the site is transformed

194
00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:24.160
into an elite proving ground
for spies.

195
00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.080
- Trainees refer to it
as "The Farm."

196
00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:30.480
And generations of spies
are secretly schooled here.

197
00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.760
right up to the present day.

198
00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:34.400
♪ ♪

199
00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.160
Training begins

200
00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:38.800
when students leave
CIA Headquarters in Langley

201
00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:40.960
on a blacked-out bus.

202
00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:42.680
- The men and women
chosen for this

203
00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:44.080
are among the most elite.

204
00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:46.400
They've gone
through rigorous testing--

205
00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.240
psychological testing.
physical testing--

206
00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.680
to prove that they are truly
the best of the best.

207
00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:54.800
[Hakeem] When a CIA trainee
arrives at The Farm.

208
00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:57.160
they leave their real identity
at the door.

209
00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:59.000
They're given a new cover story

210
00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.000
that they must maintain
throughout the training.

211
00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.200
[Andrew] They are leaving
the real world

212
00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.400
to go into a fake world.

213
00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:08.760
a fake microstate

214
00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:11.000
that simulates life
in a foreign country.

215
00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:13.520
And it's
in this simulated country

216
00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:16.000
that their
undercover training begins.

217
00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:20.920
- The whole location
of the Farm is one giant set.

218
00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.680
There's a town square.

219
00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:25.400
a shady downtown neighborhood.

220
00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:27.720
suburbs.
and then the countryside.

221
00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.240
Everyone on the site.

222
00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.720
from visiting diplomats
to the local café owner.

223
00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.840
is a veteran CIA operative
playing a role.

224
00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:37.560
There's even
a cable news channel

225
00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.560
reporting on the region's
fictional politics.

226
00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:44.040
- The Farm really is
Disney World for adults.

227
00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:45.720
[thunder rumbles]

228
00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:47.200
[Duchovny]
In this college.

229
00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.400
lessons aren't learned
in the classroom

230
00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.000
but on the streets
of its fake town.

231
00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:53.800
- The foundation
of undercover work

232
00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.840
is being able to recruit
and handle

233
00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.480
foreign intelligence sources.

234
00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.960
You're looking for people
who have access to secrets.

235
00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.560
♪ ♪

236
00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:04.400
- The whole time.
they're playing cat and mouse

237
00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.840
with their rivals and enemies--

238
00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.640
other students and operatives

239
00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:11.000
who are trying
to catch them out.

240
00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:12.680
[Duchovny]
Outfoxing the enemy

241
00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.080
calls for some of the more
advanced maneuvers

242
00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:17.640
that a wannabe James Bond
must learn.

243
00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.760
- You're trained how to flip
a car during a car chase.

244
00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.840
how to get in a firefight

245
00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:25.880
and not shoot unarmed.
innocent civilians.

246
00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.520
how to parachute
out of aircraft

247
00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:30.600
and survive in the woods
on. you know. no food.

248
00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:32.400
You learn
all the kind of things

249
00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.760
that you would see
in a spy movie.

250
00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:37.000
[Duchovny]
The new recruits are pushed

251
00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:38.920
to the edge of their wits.

252
00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:40.800
- After six months

253
00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:43.200
of intense blood. sweat.

254
00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:45.880
tears. stress. strain. anxiety.

255
00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.600
this siren blares out...
[siren blaring]

256
00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:51.960
And signals
that the simulation is over.

257
00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:55.600
and any trainees that are left
have made the cut.

258
00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:58.000
[Duchovny] The government
has never officially admitted

259
00:10:58.120 --> 00:10:59.640
