289
00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:19.800
[James] Halfway between
the prime minister's residence

290
00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.960
in Downing Street
and the British Parliament

291
00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:23.840
sits the Treasury.

292
00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:27.080
Here. they have a vast basement
ten feet below the ground.

293
00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.160
which is used
to store thousands

294
00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:31.280
of Treasury documents.

295
00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:34.080
[Duchovny]
A top secret makeover begins.

296
00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:36.360
- This underground space
beneath the Treasury

297
00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:39.960
is divided
into 70 hyper-secure rooms.

298
00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:43.200
Now. this included everything
from the cabinet office.

299
00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:46.520
offices for secretaries
and switchboard operators.

300
00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:50.760
and a dedicated bedroom
