396
00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:47.760
♪ ♪

397
00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:49.440
[Duchovny]
After World War II.

398
00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.760
the United States
engages in a race

399
00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:55.240
to stockpile the largest
arsenal of nuclear weapons.

400
00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:57.600
Building the most destructive
warheads on Earth

401
00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:00.360
requires a new kind
of top secret factory.

402
00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:04.160
a place so dangerous. it comes
with a chilling fail-safe.

403
00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:07.520
One wrong move.
and it self-destructs.

404
00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:11.400
♪ ♪

405
00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:13.160
- By the early 1950s.

406
00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:15.320
we're in the beginnings
of the Cold War.

407
00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:18.760
and both the Americans
and the Soviets have the bomb.

408
00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:21.760
So. in order
to regain nuclear superiority.

409
00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:25.080
the U.S. goes all-in
on maximizing production.

410
00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:27.840
The attitude from American
military leaders is this--

411
00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:31.320
if we can't have
the only nuclear weapons.

412
00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.960
then we have to have the most.

413
00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:36.960
[Duchovny] A few hundred
warheads won't cut it.

414
00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:39.680
The U.S. wants thousands.

415
00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:42.360
- You're creating
these things in volume.

416
00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:45.600
in a factory packed full
of volatile materials.

417
00:17:45.720 --> 00:17:48.480
One false move. and you'll have
a nuclear fireball

418
00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:50.400
on home soil.

419
00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:52.000
[Duchovny]
A site this hazardous

420
00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:55.240
needs to be remote. secure.
and secret.

421
00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:57.560
- The Atomic Energy Commission.
or the AEC.

422
00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.680
begins scouting
for suitable sites.

423
00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:02.240
One facility
that ticks all the boxes

424
00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:04.960
is an old World War II
munitions plant

425
00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:08.160
in the Texas Panhandle.
25 miles from Amarillo.

426
00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:11.360
It's called Pantex.

427
00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:14.520
During the war. thousands
of workers. mostly women.

428
00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.400
packed munitions
and shells here.

429
00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:18.640
but now the factory is closed.

430
00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:20.160
♪ ♪

431
00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.760
[Duchovny]
The AEC spends $25 million

432
00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:24.560
renovating the old factory.

433
00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:27.480
and in 1951.
the U.S. has itself

434
00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:28.760
a brand-new

435
00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:31.280
nuclear-weapons facility.

436
00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:34.520
Workers at Pantex quietly
and efficiently assemble

437
00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:37.360
the world's
most lethal product--

438
00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:40.640
while trying not
to blow themselves up.

439
00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:42.360
- Workers assembling
the warheads

440
00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:45.160
