485
00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:44.320
The slowdown
in missile production

486
00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:45.960
makes the world safer.

487
00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:48.160
But for workers at Pantex.

488
00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:51.440
the danger levels skyrocket.

489
00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.440
- Nuclear weapons
that were manufactured.

490
00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:55.720
in some cases
decades previously.

491
00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:57.920
have to come
into a manufacturer

492
00:20:58.040 --> 00:20:59.480
for disassembly.

493
00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:02.080
I can't imagine
something more stressful

494
00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:06.680
than trying to disassemble
a thermonuclear warhead.

495
00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:09.000
- Nuclear weapons aren't
designed to be disassembled.

496
00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:10.720
and some of these
have been sitting around

497
00:21:10.840 --> 00:21:12.200
for up to 40 years.

498
00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:14.560
They've degraded.
and some of their explosives

499
00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:16.800
are not as stable
as they once were.

500
00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.760
- Now it's turned over
to Pantex and go.

501
00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:20.480
here's the problem--
you solve it.

502
00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:23.800
You take it apart. and try
not to have an explosion.

503
00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:25.920
♪ ♪

504
00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:27.720
[Duchovny]
It's not just the nukes

505
00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:29.760
