their use-by date.

506
00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:32.560
[Martin] At this time.
Pantex is over 50 years old.

507
00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.800
and it's in desperate need
of an upgrade.

508
00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:37.960
but. instead. they're rushing
to complete the materials.

509
00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:39.760
[Duchovny]
The rush is so intense

510
00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:43.920
that in 1996. factory workers
blow the whistle.

511
00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:45.560
♪ ♪

512
00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:47.200
[Hakeem]
"The New York Times"

513
00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.920
publishes some astonishing
and disturbing claims

514
00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:53.120
that at Pantex.
the equipment is faulty.

515
00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:55.360
and safety measures
are being ignored.

516
00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:57.520
♪ ♪

517
00:21:57.640 --> 00:21:59.160
[Duchovny]
For the first time.

518
00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:01.360
the public is alerted
to a nuclear threat

519
00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:03.160
on their own doorstep.

520
00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:05.720
♪ ♪

521
00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:08.640
The site is still
in operation.

522
00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:11.040
with as many as 2.000 warheads

523
00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:13.600
still waiting
to be disassembled.

524
00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:15.800
♪ ♪

525
00:22:19.960 --> 00:22:21.400
- If the Soviets sent assassins

526
00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:23.400
to try and kill you not once
but 22 times.

527
00:22:23.520 --> 00:22:26.440
it makes sense to build
a secret underground hideout.

528
00:22:26.560 --> 00:22:28.840
But that doesn't mean
it can't be comfortable.

529
00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:31.200
This is the story
of how one European dictator

530
00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:33.920
commissions
his own private super bunker

531
00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:36.680
to the tune of $20 billion.

532
00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:39.960
[dramatic music]

533
00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:42.800
- After World War II.
Yugoslavia is led

534
00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:46.800
by a socialist dictator
by the name of Josip Broz.

535
00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:50.240
He is better known
to the world as Tito.

536
00:22:50.360 --> 00:22:52.000
[Duchovny]
Yugoslavia is independent

537
00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:54.920
from both Western Europe
and the Soviet Union.

538
00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:56.960
But this comes at a cost.

539
00:22:57.080 --> 00:23:00.080
Stalin hates Tito
and is out for blood.

540
00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:02.000
- The Soviet leadership
has orchestrated

541
00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.600
over 22 assassination attempts
on Tito.

542
00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:06.560
so he must be thinking.

543
00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:10.800
it's only a matter of time
until his time runs out.

544
00:23:10.920 --> 00:23:12.440
[Duchovny]
Tito believes

545
00:23:12.560 --> 00:23:14.520
a Soviet attack on Yugoslavia
is imminent.

546
00:23:14.640 --> 00:23:17.120
which would trigger
a global response.

547
00:23:17.240 --> 00:23:21.640
World War III could kick off
in his backyard.

548
00:23:21.760 --> 00:23:24.000
- Tito begins to prepare
for the worst.

549
00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:26.840
with a near-impossible
solution.

550
00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:29.680
He decides to build
an impenetrable retreat

551
00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:32.960
that has to be strong enough
to withstand a nuclear blast

552
00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:35.960
but big enough
to hold his entire government.

553
00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:38.560
[Duchovny] The only way
to meet Tito's demands

554
00:23:38.680 --> 00:23:40.480
is to tunnel under a mountain.

555
00:23:40.600 --> 00:23:43.600
- Tito's engineers pick a site
near the village of Konjic.

556
00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:45.600
and the reason is
because it's remote

557
00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:47.000
and shielded by the mountains.

558
00:23:47.120 --> 00:23:49.000
Plus. its central location

559
00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:51.200
makes it pretty accessible
for government ministers

560
00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:53.720
who are in a mad rush
to take shelter.

561
00:23:53.840 --> 00:23:55.400
[Duchovny]
The question is.

562
00:23:55.520 --> 00:23:57.800
how do you hollow out
a mountain in secret?

563
00:23:57.920 --> 00:24:00.200
- To maintain
total confidentiality.

564
00:24:00.320 --> 00:24:03.160
Tito enforces extraordinary
security protocols.

565
00:24:03.280 --> 00:24:05.000
- He does not employ locals.

566
00:24:05.120 --> 00:24:07.200
Instead. he brings in
construction workers

567
00:24:07.320 --> 00:24:08.880
from other parts
of the country

568
00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:11.200
who won't be able to recognize
the location.

569
00:24:11.320 --> 00:24:14.200
- As an extra measure.
they travel in blindfolds

570
00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:17.520
or in blacked-out vehicles
to the location.

571
00:24:17.640 --> 00:24:20.320
[Duchovny] The site is
cordoned off from the public.

572
00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:23.080
and an immense
tunneling project begins.

573
00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:26.120
♪ ♪

574
00:24:26.240 --> 00:24:27.840
- Workers are using explosives

575
00:24:27.960 --> 00:24:31.320
to slowly and methodically
burrow within the mountain.

576
00:24:31.440 --> 00:24:33.800
It's brutal and dangerous work.

577
00:24:33.920 --> 00:24:36.200
In fact.
later testimonies claim

578
00:24:36.320 --> 00:24:39.000
that barely
a single shift passes

579
00:24:39.120 --> 00:24:41.200
without someone
getting killed.

580
00:24:41.320 --> 00:24:44.600
[Duchovny] As the deaths
stack up. so does the cost.

581
00:24:44.720 --> 00:24:46.120
Tito pours the equivalent

582
00:24:46.240 --> 00:24:49.000
of $20 billion
into the tunnel.

583
00:24:49.120 --> 00:24:51.000
and meter by meter.

584
00:24:51.120 --> 00:24:53.400
his hidden fortress
takes shape.

585
00:24:53.520 --> 00:24:56.000
- The entrance
to Tito's bunker admits you

586
00:24:56.120 --> 00:24:59.480
to a horseshoe-shaped
200-meter-long tunnel

587
00:24:59.600 --> 00:25:02.040
that's carved
into the mountain.

588
00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:04.600
It has 100 dormitories

589
00:25:04.720 --> 00:25:07.000
that are capable of housing 350

590
00:25:07.120 --> 00:25:10.400
of Yugoslavia's political
and military elite.

591
00:25:10.520 --> 00:25:13.640
In every way. this facility
is designed to provide

592
00:25:13.760 --> 00:25:15.200
for the continuity
of government

593
00:25:15.320 --> 00:25:17.280
in the eventuality
of a nuclear war.

594
00:25:17.400 --> 00:25:18.800
[Duchovny]
The base is fitted out

595
00:25:18.920 --> 00:25:20.280
with the latest Cold War tech.

596
00:25:20.400 --> 00:25:22.600
- It contains
five operational centers

597
00:25:22.720 --> 00:25:24.400
with a cryptography center

598
00:25:24.520 --> 00:25:27.240
and even a fully equipped
hospital operating room.

599
00:25:27.360 --> 00:25:29.200
[Duchovny]
The most iconic gadget

600
00:25:29.320 --> 00:25:31.240
is straight
out of a spy movie--

601
00:25:31.360 --> 00:25:34.000
the red telephone.
which will ring

602
00:25:34.120 --> 00:25:36.480
when nuclear Armageddon
kicks off.

603
00:25:36.600 --> 00:25:38.200
If that happens.

604
00:25:38.320 --> 00:25:40.400
Tito can sit out
the end of the world

605
00:25:40.520 --> 00:25:42.280
in relative luxury.

606
00:25:42.400 --> 00:25:44.200
- The rest of the survivors
will have to slum it.

607
00:25:44.320 --> 00:25:46.400
but Tito gets
a private residence

608
00:25:46.520 --> 00:25:47.880
in the heart of the mountain.

609
00:25:48.000 --> 00:25:49.400
It consists of five rooms.

610
00:25:49.520 --> 00:25:51.240
including an office
and a bedroom.

611
00:25:51.360 --> 00:25:54.200
with the bunker's
only double bed.

612
00:25:54.320 --> 00:25:57.520
[Duchovny] The inside
of the bunker is vast.

613
00:25:57.640 --> 00:26:00.000
but the entrance is hidden
to the outside world

614
00:26:00.120 --> 00:26:01.440
by a stroke of genius.

615
00:26:01.560 --> 00:26:03.600
It's camouflaged
behind the façade

616
00:26:03.720 --> 00:26:06.600
of three
regular-looking houses.

617
00:26:06.720 --> 00:26:09.000
- Tito's impossible dream

618
00:26:09.120 --> 00:26:12.000
is finally completed in 1979--

619
00:26:12.120 --> 00:26:14.520
26 years
after construction began.

620
00:26:14.640 --> 00:26:18.000
[Duchovny] But Tito never gets
to take the grand tour.

621
00:26:18.120 --> 00:26:20.200
He dies in 1980.

622
00:26:20.320 --> 00:26:22.600
The secret bunker
is fully operational.

623
00:26:22.720 --> 00:26:25.800
and the Yugoslav government
keeps it on standby.

624
00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:28.880
Then. 40 years
after construction began.

625
00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:31.040
an incredible order is given--

626
00:26:31.160 --> 00:26:33.200
to blow this thing apart.

627
00:26:33.320 --> 00:26:35.240
♪ ♪

628
00:26:35.360 --> 00:26:36.840
- In the early 1990s.

629
00:26:36.960 --> 00:26:39.240
Yugoslavia.
as it used to be known.

630
00:26:39.360 --> 00:26:42.120
is torn apart
as a result of a civil war.

631
00:26:42.240 --> 00:26:45.280
And Tito's bunker is right
in the middle of the conflict.

632
00:26:45.400 --> 00:26:46.600
For the past 12 years.

633
00:26:46.720 --> 00:26:48.400
the bunker
has been looked after

634
00:26:48.520 --> 00:26:50.800
by one of Tito's
trusted servants--

635
00:26:50.920 --> 00:26:53.680
Colonel Grabovica. who's now
with the Serbian army.

636
00:26:53.800 --> 00:26:57.240
Bosnian troops are advancing
toward the complex.

637
00:26:57.360 --> 00:26:59.720
Colonel Grabovica
is given an order

638
00:26:59.840 --> 00:27:03.440
to demolish the entire
facility with explosives.

639
00:27:03.560 --> 00:27:06.000
[Sami]
This is an agonizing order.

640
00:27:06.120 --> 00:27:09.400
because Grabovica
has spent 12 years

641
00:27:09.520 --> 00:27:11.120
taking care of this complex.

642
00:27:11.240 --> 00:27:13.000
When his unit
plants the explosives

643
00:27:13.120 --> 00:27:14.640
and prepares to leave.

644
00:27:14.760 --> 00:27:16.400
he makes a decision

645
00:27:16.520 --> 00:27:19.280
that could cost him his life
for treason.

646
00:27:19.400 --> 00:27:23.000
He quietly cuts the cables
connected to the explosives.

647
00:27:23.120 --> 00:27:26.040
and he saves Tito's bunker.

648
00:27:26.160 --> 00:27:27.800
[Duchovny]
The underground complex

649
00:27:27.920 --> 00:27:30.200
is taken by Bosnian troops.

650
00:27:30.320 --> 00:27:33.000
who retain it as a secret
military installation

651
00:27:33.120 --> 00:27:35.880
until the end
of the civil war.

652
00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:39.320
In 2011. it's finally
decommissioned.

653
00:27:39.440 --> 00:27:41.000
and the government
opens its doors

654
00:27:41.120 --> 00:27:43.480
as a museum and art space.

655
00:27:43.600 --> 00:27:46.200
Locals get to explore
the secret labyrinth

656
00:27:46.320 --> 00:27:50.160
that's been hiding behind
these houses for 60 years.

657
00:27:55.200 --> 00:27:56.960
- A quiet neighborhood
in Germany

658
00:27:57.080 --> 00:28:00.520
is the last place you'd expect
to find a sinister CIA program.

659
00:28:00.640 --> 00:28:04.880
It's a site that brings
together Soviet spies. LSD.

660
00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:09.240
and a Nazi scientist intent
on mastering mind control.

661
00:28:09.360 --> 00:28:12.880
[dramatic music]

662
00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.280
[Martin] During the early
years of the Cold War.

663
00:28:15.400 --> 00:28:18.080
the CIA is more
and more obsessed

664
00:28:18.200 --> 00:28:19.840
with interrogation techniques.

665
00:28:19.960 --> 00:28:21.920
They want to be able
to manipulate the enemy

666
00:28:22.040 --> 00:28:23.480
who falls into our hands.

667
00:28:23.600 --> 00:28:25.880
and then they also
want to figure out ways

668
00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:28.120
to reinforce the will

669
00:28:28.240 --> 00:28:30.400
of our personnel who might fall
into enemy hands.

670
00:28:30.520 --> 00:28:31.880
reinforce their ability

671
00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:34.080
to resist
interrogation techniques

672
00:28:34.200 --> 00:28:35.880
that the enemy
might expose them to.

673
00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:38.280
The only way to figure out
how best to serve

674
00:28:38.400 --> 00:28:39.920
both of those masters

675
00:28:40.040 --> 00:28:42.160
is to conduct
psychological experiments.

676
00:28:42.280 --> 00:28:44.920
[Duchovny] The CIA sets up
a top secret program

677
00:28:45.040 --> 00:28:47.120
to explore methods
of mind control.

678
00:28:47.240 --> 00:28:50.800
It's called Project Bluebird.

679
00:28:50.920 --> 00:28:52.880
- These experiments
can't be conducted

680
00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:54.880
in a regular laboratory.
obviously.

681
00:28:55.000 --> 00:28:57.320
They have to be done
in a classified environment--

682
00:28:57.440 --> 00:28:58.800
a sort of black site

683
00:28:58.920 --> 00:29:00.880
that governments
typically turn a blind eye to.

684
00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:04.680
[Duchovny] So Project Bluebird
is taken out of the U.S..

685
00:29:04.800 --> 00:29:07.000
to battle-scarred
West Germany.

686
00:29:07.120 --> 00:29:09.080
- At this time.
part of Germany is still

687
00:29:09.200 --> 00:29:11.520
under American occupation
after World War II.

688
00:29:11.640 --> 00:29:13.480
when the U.S. military
have a site

689
00:29:13.600 --> 00:29:16.480
in a quiet town
just north of Frankfurt.

690
00:29:16.600 --> 00:29:19.000
[Duchovny]
It's called Camp King.

691
00:29:19.120 --> 00:29:20.960
- Camp King has been in use
since World War II.

692
00:29:21.080 --> 00:29:22.680
It was used for imprisoning

693
00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:24.680
and interrogating
Nazi leaders.

694
00:29:24.800 --> 00:29:27.200
[Sasha] Camp King has
the perfect infrastructure

695
00:29:27.320 --> 00:29:29.960
for psychological experiments.

696
00:29:30.080 --> 00:29:33.400
It has secure cells.
housing for staff.

697
00:29:33.520 --> 00:29:35.080
and even a hospital.

698
00:29:35.200 --> 00:29:37.280
[Duchovny]
But its most vital asset--

699
00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:39.080
absolute privacy.

700
00:29:39.200 --> 00:29:41.480
- The locals are used to seeing
the Americans

701
00:29:41.600 --> 00:29:43.880
from Camp King around.
and they don't ask questions

702
00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:45.880
about what
they're doing inside.

703
00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:48.400
[Duchovny] The project needs
a lead scientist.

704
00:29:48.520 --> 00:29:50.880
someone willing to turn
a blind eye

705
00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:53.120
to medical ethics.

706
00:29:53.240 --> 00:29:55.600
- It turns out that the chief
medical doctor at Camp King

707
00:29:55.720 --> 00:29:57.400
has quite the résumé.

708
00:29:57.520 --> 00:30:00.920
Dr. Walter Schreiber
is the former surgeon general

709
00:30:01.040 --> 00:30:02.320
of the German army.

710
00:30:02.440 --> 00:30:04.480
- Walter Schreiber oversaw

711
00:30:04.600 --> 00:30:06.520
horrific medical experiments

712
00:30:06.640 --> 00:30:08.280
at Dachau and Auschwitz.

713
00:30:08.400 --> 00:30:09.760
Under his watch.

714
00:30:09.880 --> 00:30:13.120
concentration camp prisoners
are frozen.

715
00:30:13.240 --> 00:30:15.480
injected with hallucinogens.

716
00:30:15.600 --> 00:30:18.960
and even dissected
to track gangrene--

717
00:30:19.080 --> 00:30:22.960
experiments that end
in slow and painful death.

718
00:30:23.080 --> 00:30:24.880
[Duchovny]
Schreiber was picked up

719
00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:28.320
by U.S. military intelligence
after the war.

720
00:30:28.440 --> 00:30:31.920
Now his skills are put to use
on Project Bluebird.

721
00:30:32.040 --> 00:30:36.000
running Camp King's
experiments in mind control.

722
00:30:36.120 --> 00:30:38.280
- This includes
hallucinogenic drugs.

723
00:30:38.400 --> 00:30:40.000
It includes hypnosis.

724
00:30:40.120 --> 00:30:44.080
The idea is to break
the prisoner from his own mind

725
00:30:44.200 --> 00:30:46.520
and do what the CIA wants.

726
00:30:46.640 --> 00:30:49.360
[Duchovny] The secure facility
has a ready supply

727
00:30:49.480 --> 00:30:51.000
of test subjects.

728
00:30:51.120 --> 00:30:54.400
- Its current inmates
are Soviet defectors.

729
00:30:54.520 --> 00:30:56.560
spies. and refugees--

730
00:30:56.680 --> 00:30:59.840
people who could be considered
expendable.

731
00:30:59.960 --> 00:31:02.640
They could be treated
inhumanely

732
00:31:02.760 --> 00:31:06.120
or die during trials.
and who would know?

733
00:31:06.240 --> 00:31:07.680
- The subjects are described

734
00:31:07.800 --> 00:31:10.880
as experienced
professional-type agents...

735
00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:13.960
suspected of working
for Soviet intelligence.

736
00:31:14.080 --> 00:31:16.880
In one case.
doses of drugs and hypnosis

737
00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:19.600
induce a deep trance.

738
00:31:19.720 --> 00:31:21.880
One spy remains under
for two hours

739
00:31:22.000 --> 00:31:25.120
and then completely forgets
the experience.

740
00:31:25.240 --> 00:31:28.880
[Duchovny] But mastering
mind control proves elusive.

741
00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:31.080
so new instruments
are brought in.

742
00:31:31.200 --> 00:31:33.760
and the facility
expands its operations.

743
00:31:33.880 --> 00:31:35.920
[Sami] They generate
a new set of tests

744
00:31:36.040 --> 00:31:37.520
to try on their subjects.

745
00:31:37.640 --> 00:31:40.520
including exposure to gases.

746
00:31:40.640 --> 00:31:42.720
irradiation by infrared
and ultraviolet light.

747
00:31:42.840 --> 00:31:44.880
pressure chambers.
sonic torture.

748
00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:46.800
and dietary manipulation.

749
00:31:46.920 --> 00:31:49.480
Prisoners are often subjected
to multiple combinations

750
00:31:49.600 --> 00:31:52.440
of these experiments
until they can't take any more.

751
00:31:52.560 --> 00:31:56.000
[monitor flatlines]

752
00:31:56.120 --> 00:31:57.960
- Experiments
at Camp King continue

753
00:31:58.080 --> 00:31:59.880
for the rest of the decade.

754
00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.440
when they are quietly drawn
to a close.

755
00:32:02.560 --> 00:32:06.760
But the CIA's obsession
with drugs and hypnosis

756
00:32:06.880 --> 00:32:08.680
is far from over.

757
00:32:08.800 --> 00:32:11.080
[Martin] The experiments
with mind control

758
00:32:11.200 --> 00:32:12.920
inform the administration

759
00:32:13.040 --> 00:32:17.680
of the mother of all Cold War
psychological projects...

760
00:32:17.800 --> 00:32:18.960
♪ ♪

761
00:32:19.080 --> 00:32:20.800
MKUltra.

762
00:32:20.920 --> 00:32:23.880
[Duchovny] In 1993.
the U.S. returns Camp King

763
00:32:24.000 --> 00:32:27.320
to the German government.
who build houses on the site.

764
00:32:27.440 --> 00:32:31.280
Families move in. oblivious
to its gruesome history.

765
00:32:31.400 --> 00:32:32.880
until 2002.

766
00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:35.880
when German researchers
uncover the full details

767
00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:38.000
of Camp King's experiments.

768
00:32:38.120 --> 00:32:39.760
♪ ♪

769
00:32:39.880 --> 00:32:42.680
And the new residents learn
the terrifying truth

770
00:32:42.800 --> 00:32:45.480
about the place
they now call home.

771
00:32:49.640 --> 00:32:51.200
- In the 1940s.

772
00:32:51.320 --> 00:32:53.200
the U.S. sets up a weapons
research lab in Los Alamos

773
00:32:53.320 --> 00:32:55.200
that covers
a sprawling 40 square miles.

774
00:32:55.320 --> 00:32:56.880
But the Soviets--

775
00:32:57.000 --> 00:33:00.000
they go bigger.
75 times bigger.

776
00:33:00.120 --> 00:33:04.040
with a secret weapons facility
3.000 square miles in size.

777
00:33:04.160 --> 00:33:06.720
The question is.
how do you keep that hidden?

778
00:33:06.840 --> 00:33:10.800
[dramatic music]

779
00:33:10.920 --> 00:33:12.440
[Martin]
By the end of World War II.

780
00:33:12.560 --> 00:33:15.120
both the United States
and the Soviet Union

781
00:33:15.240 --> 00:33:17.600
recognize that missiles
will dominate

782
00:33:17.720 --> 00:33:19.040
the future battlefield.

783
00:33:19.160 --> 00:33:20.720
♪ ♪

784
00:33:20.840 --> 00:33:23.120
The Soviets have captured
existing examples

785
00:33:23.240 --> 00:33:24.600
of the German V-2 rocket--

786
00:33:24.720 --> 00:33:26.520
the world's
first ballistic missile.

787
00:33:26.640 --> 00:33:30.520
In addition to that. they have
captured German scientists.

788
00:33:30.640 --> 00:33:33.960
The Soviets want to use
the V-2 rockets

789
00:33:34.080 --> 00:33:37.280
to help them develop
a new missile defense system.

790
00:33:37.400 --> 00:33:38.800
[Duchovny]
The problem is.

791
00:33:38.920 --> 00:33:40.760
they have nowhere
to launch them.

792
00:33:40.880 --> 00:33:42.600
[Greg] They want to test
these bad boys out.

793
00:33:42.720 --> 00:33:44.200
The thing is.
they've got to do this

794
00:33:44.320 --> 00:33:46.240
away from the eyes of the West.

795
00:33:46.360 --> 00:33:49.920
They need something private.
something secure.

796
00:33:50.040 --> 00:33:51.800
[Duchovny]
In May 1946.

797
00:33:51.920 --> 00:33:54.400
Soviet command
signs off the location

798
00:33:54.520 --> 00:33:56.400
of their new facility.

799
00:33:56.520 --> 00:33:58.400
And to ensure total secrecy.

800
00:33:58.520 --> 00:34:00.600
it's in one
of the most isolated stretches

801
00:34:00.720 --> 00:34:02.280
of the country.

802
00:34:02.400 --> 00:34:04.560
- The Soviets choose
a remote location in the south.

803
00:34:04.680 --> 00:34:07.680
in the desert. very close
to the Kazakh border.

804
00:34:07.800 --> 00:34:09.680
at a place
called Kapustin Yar.

805
00:34:09.800 --> 00:34:13.520
It's 600 miles from Moscow and
60 miles from the nearest town.

806
00:34:13.640 --> 00:34:14.960
♪ ♪

807
00:34:15.080 --> 00:34:16.960
[Duchovny]
The extreme isolation

808
00:34:17.080 --> 00:34:20.440
is its major selling point
and biggest problem.

809
00:34:20.560 --> 00:34:24.000
- There's no roads.
no rail. no power.

810
00:34:24.120 --> 00:34:27.000
I mean. there's nothing
out there but empty horizon.

811
00:34:27.120 --> 00:34:30.040
which is perfect for secrecy
and volatile rocket tests.

812
00:34:30.160 --> 00:34:32.400
but it's terrible for
a massive construction project

813
00:34:32.520 --> 00:34:34.000
on an ambitious deadline.

814
00:34:34.120 --> 00:34:36.000
[Greg] It's also
a horrendous place to work.

815
00:34:36.120 --> 00:34:38.080
In the summer.
temperatures can get

816
00:34:38.200 --> 00:34:39.800
well over
100 degrees Fahrenheit.

817
00:34:39.920 --> 00:34:42.000
and in the winter.
it plummets to below freezing.

818
00:34:42.120 --> 00:34:44.000
[Duchovny] But Stalin
wants rockets in the sky

819
00:34:44.120 --> 00:34:46.400
as soon as possible.
so he hands the project

820
00:34:46.520 --> 00:34:48.320
to one
of his finest commanders--

821
00:34:48.440 --> 00:34:51.640
General
Vasily Ivanovich Voznyuk.

822
00:34:51.760 --> 00:34:55.240
- Voznyuk is a man who thrives
on the impossible.

823
00:34:55.360 --> 00:34:57.760
He's legendary
for his iron will

824
00:34:57.880 --> 00:34:59.880
and genius for logistics.

825
00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:03.120
♪ ♪

826
00:35:03.240 --> 00:35:05.480
[Amy] Voznyuk is sent
to this remote site.

827
00:35:05.600 --> 00:35:07.080
and he immediately
gets to work.

828
00:35:07.200 --> 00:35:09.600
He builds a tent city
to house all the workers

829
00:35:09.720 --> 00:35:11.800
and then builds roads
and rail lines

830
00:35:11.920 --> 00:35:13.960
to bring in all
the construction material

831
00:35:14.080 --> 00:35:16.480
they're going to need
to make this base a reality.

832
00:35:16.600 --> 00:35:18.080
[Duchovny]
Voznyuk's team

833
00:35:18.200 --> 00:35:20.320
may be sleeping in tents
on the desert floor.

834
00:35:20.440 --> 00:35:22.200
but in just two months.

835
00:35:22.320 --> 00:35:24.440
they built a launchpad
and a command center.

836
00:35:24.560 --> 00:35:27.800
The new Soviet weapons program
is ready for takeoff.

837
00:35:27.920 --> 00:35:29.800
- In October of 1947.

838
00:35:29.920 --> 00:35:32.000
the secret base at Kapustin Yar

839
00:35:32.120 --> 00:35:33.960
launches
its first-ever rocket--

840
00:35:34.080 --> 00:35:36.200
a refurbished German V-2

841
00:35:36.320 --> 00:35:39.320
that flies
for almost 200 kilometers.

842
00:35:39.440 --> 00:35:41.600
After that.
the Kapustin Yar base

843
00:35:41.720 --> 00:35:43.160
expands rapidly.

844
00:35:43.280 --> 00:35:45.120
A new town is completed.

845
00:35:45.240 --> 00:35:48.280
and it becomes the cradle
of Soviet missile development.

846
00:35:48.400 --> 00:35:51.320
all hidden from Western eyes.

847
00:35:51.440 --> 00:35:54.400
- In the Cold War.
nothing remains secret forever.

848
00:35:54.520 --> 00:35:56.320
Whispers
of a Soviet missile base

849
00:35:56.440 --> 00:35:58.200
send Western governments
scrambling

850
00:35:58.320 --> 00:35:59.920
for photographic evidence.

851
00:36:00.040 --> 00:36:03.840
And in 1959. the British
sneak across the Iron Curtain--

852
00:36:03.960 --> 00:36:06.000
or rather. above it.

853
00:36:06.120 --> 00:36:08.320
♪ ♪

854
00:36:08.440 --> 00:36:12.240
- On December 6. 1959.
a British pilot sets off

855
00:36:12.360 --> 00:36:13.800
towards the Soviet desert.

856
00:36:13.920 --> 00:36:15.640
[Greg]
They're flying an aircraft

857
00:36:15.760 --> 00:36:18.360
that the world
has never seen--the U-2.

858
00:36:18.480 --> 00:36:21.240
[Amy] The U-2 is the pinnacle
in aerial espionage.

859
00:36:21.360 --> 00:36:23.400
It's designed to fly so high

860
00:36:23.520 --> 00:36:25.200
with such
high-resolution cameras

861
00:36:25.320 --> 00:36:27.800
that it should be able
to photograph this new site

862
00:36:27.920 --> 00:36:29.800
while staying
clear out of the way

863
00:36:29.920 --> 00:36:31.760
of any possible
Soviet missiles.

864
00:36:31.880 --> 00:36:33.200
♪ ♪

865
00:36:33.320 --> 00:36:36.320
- He passes
right over Soviet territory.

866
00:36:36.440 --> 00:36:37.880
and he comes back

867
00:36:38.000 --> 00:36:40.120
with the first
high-quality photographs

868
00:36:40.240 --> 00:36:43.480
of Kapustin Yar
to reach the West.

869
00:36:43.600 --> 00:36:45.400
- The photos collected
by the U-2

870
00:36:45.520 --> 00:36:47.280
are absolutely critical.

871
00:36:47.400 --> 00:36:48.920
They tell the Western Allies

872
00:36:49.040 --> 00:36:50.560
exactly what type
of technology

873
00:36:50.680 --> 00:36:52.480
the Soviets have developed.

874
00:36:52.600 --> 00:36:55.040
They tell them exactly what
type of fuel they're using.

875
00:36:55.160 --> 00:36:57.160
they tell them vital things
that they need to know

876
00:36:57.280 --> 00:37:00.360
about Soviet missile technology
and capability.

877
00:37:00.480 --> 00:37:02.000
♪ ♪

878
00:37:02.120 --> 00:37:05.320
[Duchovny] Kapustin Yar
is no longer a secret...

879
00:37:05.440 --> 00:37:07.200
giving the West a vital window

880
00:37:07.320 --> 00:37:10.560
into the Soviet
missile program.

881
00:37:10.680 --> 00:37:13.680
But U.S. surveillance
doesn't slow down progress.

882
00:37:13.800 --> 00:37:16.240
The desert base
continues its operation

883
00:37:16.360 --> 00:37:18.200
and remains the beating heart

884
00:37:18.320 --> 00:37:21.320
of Russian weapons
innovations today.

885
00:37:25.440 --> 00:37:26.600
- There's a facility in Utah

886
00:37:26.720 --> 00:37:28.360
that's bigger
than the Pentagon.

887
00:37:28.480 --> 00:37:30.360
with restricted access.
no windows.

888
00:37:30.480 --> 00:37:31.880
and a secret objective--

889
00:37:32.000 --> 00:37:34.600
reportedly to spy on us all.

890
00:37:34.720 --> 00:37:38.200
[dramatic music]

891
00:37:38.320 --> 00:37:39.680
- In the early 2010s.

892
00:37:39.800 --> 00:37:42.160
deep on the salt flats
of Bluffdale. Utah.

893
00:37:42.280 --> 00:37:45.560
construction begins on
a sprawling 240-acre complex.

894
00:37:45.680 --> 00:37:47.560
Now. this is not
a secret complex.

895
00:37:47.680 --> 00:37:49.480
It can't be a secret.

896
00:37:49.600 --> 00:37:51.680
The place is over 50 times
the size of the U.S. Capitol.

897
00:37:51.800 --> 00:37:54.040
Officially. this complex is
known

898
00:37:54.160 --> 00:37:55.960
as the Intelligence Community

899
00:37:56.080 --> 00:37:57.520
Comprehensive
National Cybersecurity

900
00:37:57.640 --> 00:37:59.040
Initiative Data Center.

901
00:37:59.160 --> 00:38:01.840
Locals just call it
the "Utah Data Center."

902
00:38:01.960 --> 00:38:05.440
- This giant complex is
a National Security Agency site

903
00:38:05.560 --> 00:38:06.760
for cyber defense.

904
00:38:06.880 --> 00:38:08.840
Today surveillance. sabotage.

905
00:38:08.960 --> 00:38:11.640
and even terrorist attacks
can be carried out remotely.

906
00:38:11.760 --> 00:38:13.560
The NSA says
the Utah Data Center

907
00:38:13.680 --> 00:38:17.160
is designed to protect everyday
Americans from cyberattacks.

908
00:38:17.280 --> 00:38:19.360
[Duchovny] The latest
sprawling data facility

909
00:38:19.480 --> 00:38:20.960
barely makes the headlines.

910
00:38:21.080 --> 00:38:23.480
which might be just
what the NSA wants.

911
00:38:23.600 --> 00:38:25.560
until journalists
begin to question

912
00:38:25.680 --> 00:38:28.600
the unprecedented scale
of the site.

913
00:38:28.720 --> 00:38:30.360
- At the heart
of the construction.

914
00:38:30.480 --> 00:38:32.320
four vast data halls
are being built.

915
00:38:32.440 --> 00:38:35.560
each 25.000 square feet.

916
00:38:35.680 --> 00:38:36.760
These will be filled

917
00:38:36.880 --> 00:38:38.160
with cutting-edge computer

918
00:38:38.280 --> 00:38:39.640
servers and hardware

919
00:38:39.760 --> 00:38:43.400
that will devour
65 megawatts of power.

920
00:38:43.520 --> 00:38:45.560
- It will come
with an electricity bill

921
00:38:45.680 --> 00:38:48.760
of $40 million a year.

922
00:38:48.880 --> 00:38:50.960
and keeping those servers
from overheating

923
00:38:51.080 --> 00:38:55.840
requires 1.7 million gallons
of water every day.

924
00:38:55.960 --> 00:38:58.160
[Duchovny]
It's a technological marvel

925
00:38:58.280 --> 00:39:01.040
that you can't see
without top-level clearance.

926
00:39:01.160 --> 00:39:03.320
- Security is fortress level.

927
00:39:03.440 --> 00:39:06.760
with biometric access.
24-7 surveillance.

928
00:39:06.880 --> 00:39:09.960
and barriers that can stop
a 15.000-pound truck

929
00:39:10.080 --> 00:39:12.280
moving at 50 miles per hour.

930
00:39:12.400 --> 00:39:14.560
[Duchovny]
So why all the secrecy?

931
00:39:14.680 --> 00:39:16.760
[Sasha] When journalists
crunch the numbers.

932
00:39:16.880 --> 00:39:19.160
they realize
that the Utah Data Center

933
00:39:19.280 --> 00:39:22.800
can store an unimaginable
amount of data.

934
00:39:22.920 --> 00:39:24.960
Some estimate
it's yottabytes--

935
00:39:25.080 --> 00:39:26.840
a trillion terabytes.

936
00:39:26.960 --> 00:39:28.920
[Duchovny]
To put that into context.

937
00:39:29.040 --> 00:39:32.040
that's the equivalent
of 2 trillion laptops.

938
00:39:32.160 --> 00:39:34.360
- This site could hold
more information

939
00:39:34.480 --> 00:39:36.080
than we ever thought possible

940
00:39:36.200 --> 00:39:39.000
and still have space for more.

941
00:39:39.120 --> 00:39:40.920
[Duchovny]
It begs the question--

942
00:39:41.040 --> 00:39:45.120
what exactly is the NSA going
to store on those servers?

943
00:39:45.240 --> 00:39:47.680
In 2012. journalists
for "The New York Times"

944
00:39:47.800 --> 00:39:49.360
pick up the trail.

945
00:39:49.480 --> 00:39:51.800
when a retired
NSA technical director

946
00:39:51.920 --> 00:39:55.000
named William Binney
steps out of the shadows

947
00:39:55.120 --> 00:39:57.200
and blows the whistle.

948
00:39:57.320 --> 00:39:59.760
[Amy] In the late 90s.
Binney created a program

949
00:39:59.880 --> 00:40:01.200
called ThinThread

950
00:40:01.320 --> 00:40:02.960
that searched everything
on the Internet

951
00:40:03.080 --> 00:40:05.120
for anything
that was potentially harmful.

952
00:40:05.240 --> 00:40:07.600
like terrorist attacks
or any other security attacks.

953
00:40:07.720 --> 00:40:09.760
[Sami] His program
protects the privacy

954
00:40:09.880 --> 00:40:12.680
of innocent civilians
by encrypting anything

955
00:40:12.800 --> 00:40:14.160
that isn't suspicious.

956
00:40:14.280 --> 00:40:16.320
while honing in
on potential bad guys.

957
00:40:16.440 --> 00:40:19.160
- Binney claims
that after 9/11.

958
00:40:19.280 --> 00:40:21.360
the safeguards were removed

959
00:40:21.480 --> 00:40:23.760
and parts of ThinThread
were used

960
00:40:23.880 --> 00:40:26.360
in a sweeping
surveillance program

961
00:40:26.480 --> 00:40:28.880
on all U.S. citizens.

962
00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:30.760
[Duchovny]
In August 2012.

963
00:40:30.880 --> 00:40:34.120
"The New York Times" publishes
Binney's revelations.

964
00:40:34.240 --> 00:40:35.560
♪ ♪

965
00:40:35.680 --> 00:40:38.160
- He contends
that the Utah Data Center

966
00:40:38.280 --> 00:40:41.520
is part of a massive
government effort

967
00:40:41.640 --> 00:40:45.320
to store troves of data
collected on Americans

968
00:40:45.440 --> 00:40:48.640
without warrants
and against the Constitution.

969
00:40:48.760 --> 00:40:50.680
[keys clacking]

970
00:40:50.800 --> 00:40:52.480
[Duchovny]
According to Binney.

971
00:40:52.600 --> 00:40:55.840
every message you send
is recorded. saved.

972
00:40:55.960 --> 00:40:59.880
and stored at places
like the Utah Data Center.

973
00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:03.280
- Allegedly. it's the last part
of the NSA's mission

974
00:41:03.400 --> 00:41:05.560
to own every digital
communication

975
00:41:05.680 --> 00:41:06.840
without oversight

976
00:41:06.960 --> 00:41:09.040
and be accessed
by NSA analysts

977
00:41:09.160 --> 00:41:11.000
all over the country.

978
00:41:11.120 --> 00:41:13.360
[Duchovny] The secret activity
in those immense data halls

979
00:41:13.480 --> 00:41:15.360
remains highly controversial.

980
00:41:15.480 --> 00:41:17.760
To its supporters.
it plays a vital role

981
00:41:17.880 --> 00:41:20.120
in keeping the country safe.

982
00:41:20.240 --> 00:41:24.000
To its detractors.
it's the real-world embodiment

983
00:41:24.120 --> 00:41:25.480
of Big Brother.

984
00:41:25.600 --> 00:41:26.920
♪ ♪

985
00:41:27.040 --> 00:41:28.960
From impenetrable bunkers

986
00:41:29.080 --> 00:41:31.240
to high-security science labs.

987
00:41:31.360 --> 00:41:34.160
governments perform
their most covert activities

988
00:41:34.280 --> 00:41:37.840
behind gates and fences
in top secret sites.

989
00:41:37.960 --> 00:41:40.800
But no door
stays locked forever.

990
00:41:40.920 --> 00:41:43.160
And the truth gets out
in the end.

991
00:41:43.280 --> 00:41:44.800
♪ ♪
